AAHP Protocol + Token Saving Guide

AAHP = AI Agent Handoff Protocol

It enables multiple AI agents (Claude / Codex / GPT) to collaborate on a codebase with minimal token usage.

Goal

Without AAHP:

agent loads entire repo
context explodes
tokens wasted

With AAHP:

agent loads only needed files
uses summaries
uses task briefs

Result:

80–95% token savings
AAHP Directory
.ai/
  handoff/
    manifest.json
    summaries/
    task_briefs/
    decisions/
    checksums/
manifest.json

Defines which files agents may read.

Example:

{
 "context_files": [
  "services/strategy-service/",
  "libs/contracts/",
  "docs/architecture.md"
 ],
 "max_context_tokens": 6000
}
Task Briefs

Each AI task has a short brief.

Example:

task: implement policy-service

context:
- libs/contracts/policy_models.py
- services/policy-service/

output:
- rule engine

constraints:
- deterministic
- audit logging

This prevents the AI from loading the entire repo.

Summaries

After each task the AI writes:

.ai/handoff/summaries/

Example summary:

policy service implemented
rules added:
- max position size
- stale data rejection

Future agents read this instead of full history.

Decision Logs
.ai/handoff/decisions/

Stores architecture decisions.

Example:

ADR-001
Execution service separated from LLM
Checksums

Ensures agents read the correct file versions.

.ai/handoff/checksums/
Token Saving Strategies
1. Context Budgeting

Example:

max tokens per task = 6000
2. File-Level Context

Load only required files.

Example:

services/policy-service/*

NOT the entire repo.

3. Structured Outputs

Agents communicate using JSON.

Example:

SignalCandidate
PolicyDecision
ExecutionOrder

Instead of paragraphs.

4. Replay Logs

Agents read summaries instead of history.

5. Prompt Templates

Reusable prompts reduce tokens.

Example AI Workflow

Agent 1

task: create policy service
reads:
- contracts
- policy service folder

Agent 2

task: add new risk rule
reads:
- summary
- policy service

Agent 3

task: add execution adapter
reads:
- execution service
